win on p9web (github.com/cptaffe/plan9web): Plan 9's win, as this tree has it (9legacy's), on
Plan 9's libthread and lib9p, objtype wasm (plan9web's mk/n9). p9web's Acme is a fork with
plan9port's ways: the changes are for it.

Changes for p9web:
	main.c	output is held until it goes in under seq (wput)
	win.c	output goes in under the window's seq (wguard, wput)
	win.c	a window is libacme's Win (acme(2)), so an amux(4) session where amux runs
	main.c	execevent takes libacme's Event, its expansion and argument in it
	main.c	the command gets an amux session of its own as /dev/acme, or /mnt/wsys/$id
	fs.c	output goes on the channel as a Msg, beside acme's events

win serves cons and consctl (lib9p) and mounts them before /dev in its namespace; rc reads and
writes them. A note to rc's note group is an interrupt (Del, or ^C).
